• Assurer la collecte des remontées utilisateurs pour apporter une dynamique d’amélioration continue sur le périmètre à sa main mais aussi pour rédiger et promouvoir auprès des équipes globales les demandes d’évolutions identifiées en se coordonnant avec les autres pays Européens ;

• Piloter et/ou assurer les développements correctifs et évolutifs du système avec l’aide des équipes globales, y compris le recettage et la validation de la stabilité des systèmes et des interfaces post-production.

Accompagnement utilisateur et promotion des bonnes pratiques

• Produire, délivrer et mettre à jour des Guides et Supports Utilisateurs des systèmes d’engagement clients ;

• Réaliser et décliner un plan de communications sur la valeur ajoutée des systèmes d’engagement clients ;

• Définir des parcours d’apprenants par profil et mettre en place des solutions de formation des utilisateurs allant du onboarding à la consolidation des acquis tout au long du cycle de vie des applications de gestion de la relation clients et de l’engagement omnicanal ;

• Améliorer la qualité des interactions et des insights saisis par des actions de formations et de conduite de changement ;

• Gérer les incidents sur l’écosystème avec l’équipe du Service Desk et les équipes globales impliquées ;

• Assurer et consolider les connaissances du Service Desk pour garantir un support de qualité.

Votre profil

• Expérience confirmée dans la gestion de systèmes d’engagement clients ;

• Expérience significative dans le paramétrage et/ou développement d’une solution

jobs.description:
At Roche you can show up as yourself, embraced for the unique qualities you bring. Our culture encourages personal expression, open dialogue, and genuine connections, where you are valued, accepted and respected for who you are, allowing you to thrive both personally and professionally. This is how we aim to prevent, stop and cure diseases and ensure everyone has access to healthcare today and for generations to come. Join Roche, where every voice matters.

The Position
We advance science so that we all have more time with the people we love.
Healthcare is changing- radical innovation, increased openness to change, increasing patient empowerment, multiple sources of medical information, and pressure on public spending. As a result of all this, the needs of our stakeholders and how we engage them continue to evolve.
Roche is looking for a Finance Director, an enabling team member primarily responsible to be a strategic thought partner and advisor to the affiliate on strategy, performance, resource allocation, commercial decisions and strategic planning. As a natural leader, you are expected to leverage a strong entrepreneurial mindset with excellent business acumen with responsibility to deliver the tender contracting business targets, deliver financial governance, develop business plans and provide analytical insight and business judgment to support strategic and tactical initiatives across the affiliate. The Finance Director will lead key affiliate functions including finance, supply chain, tenders, procurement, operational pricing (including mature product portfolio).

Your Opportunity

• Formulate a local finance strategy balancing global /PI requirements with affiliate priorities;

• Foster a close business collaborating approach to address the needs of the business and its strategy whilst taking into account the broader implications from an enterprise perspective;

• Act as key advisor to Pakistan Enabling Team by reviewing overall commercial, access and medical activities and financial performance against targets, identifying opportunities, developing proposals on improvements, assessing proposals and making recommendations on strategies to be implemented as required;

• Manage operational performance by tracking performance against targets, identifying anomalies and implementing corrective action as and when required;

• Lead commercial tendering business across Pakistan ensuring close collaboration with therapy area teams ensuring collaboration and commercial excellence;

• Lead pricing strategies for the complete portfolio including any new launches; managing the transfer pricing every year ensuring local profitability while adhering to the transfer pricing guidelines.

• Develop financial strategies that ensure compliance, and enable the delivery of more medicines to patients faster;

• Oversee the affiliate procurement process, with focus on value delivery for Roche, balancing costs, service quality, compliance and strategic partnerships;

• Oversee the local finance & accounting function, ensuring adherence to Roche Group Accounting, local accounting standards, tax and customs;

• Oversee the supply chain process ensuring a timely and efficient delivery of our drugs;

• Cultivate a focus on personal development whilst creating and nurturing a winning team through coaching and leadership;

• Oversee operations and governance of Patient Support programs

• Be an active member of the Finance Network and contribute to enterprise outcomes beyond Pakistan

• Ensure compliance of all Finance practices within the area of responsibility and beyond.

• Responsible to report incident / accident immediately to SHE department. Attend / complete all requisite on-line and F2F trainings (Role specific, Safety Responsibility and Compliance) within specified time limit.

Who you are:

• You have a minimum of 7 years of finance experience and (preferably) holds a professional accounting qualification (CPA, CA, ACA, CIMA) or a Post-gr

